<a name="h-02"></a>
## H-02 — Wrong Divisor in `closePot` Permanently Locks Unclaimed Rewards

**Severity:** High  
**Scope:** `Pot.sol`

---

### # `i_players.length` as Divisor But `claimants.length` as Loop Bound → Residual Tokens Locked Forever

### Description

* When the 90-day claim window expires, the owner calls `closePot()`. The function takes 10% as a manager cut, then is supposed to distribute the remaining 90% equally among players who claimed in time (stored in `claimants[]`).

* `claimantCut` is divided by `i_players.length` (all registered players) but the distribution loop only iterates over `claimants.length` (only those who already called `claimCut`). The residual `(i_players.length − claimants.length) × claimantCut` is never sent anywhere and has no recovery path — permanently locked in the contract. In the worst case where no player has claimed, 90% of the entire reward pool is trapped.

```solidity
function closePot() external onlyOwner {
    if (block.timestamp - i_deployedAt < 90 days) {
        revert Pot__StillOpenForClaim();
    }
    if (remainingRewards > 0) {
        uint256 managerCut = remainingRewards / managerCutPercent;
        i_token.transfer(msg.sender, managerCut);

        // @> Divides by ALL registered players (i_players.length)...
        uint256 claimantCut = (remainingRewards - managerCut) / i_players.length;
        // @> ...but only distributes to those who already claimed (claimants.length)
        for (uint256 i = 0; i < claimants.length; i++) {
            _transferReward(claimants[i], claimantCut);
        }
        // @> No residual sweep — (i_players.length - claimants.length) * claimantCut locked forever
    }
}
```

### Risk

**Likelihood:**

* Any contest where fewer players claim than total registered triggers the lock — which is the protocol's primary expected scenario (the 90-day window exists precisely because not all players claim)
* Every single `closePot` call where `claimants.length < i_players.length` permanently locks funds

**Impact:**

* Tokens equal to `(i_players.length − claimants.length) × claimantCut` are permanently locked with no withdrawal function
* In the zero-claimant case, 90% of all deposited rewards are irrecoverable
* Combined with H-01, a single normal `closeContest` call locks 100% of remaining rewards

### Proof of Concept

```solidity
function testWrongDivisorLocksTokens() public mintAndApproveTokens {
    // 5 players, each allocated 200 tokens, totalRewards = 1000
    address[] memory fivePlayers = new address[](5);
    uint256[] memory fiveRewards = new uint256[](5);
    for (uint256 i = 0; i < 5; i++) {
        fivePlayers[i] = address(uint160(i + 1));
        fiveRewards[i] = 200;
    }

    vm.startPrank(user);
    contest = ContestManager(conMan).createContest(
        fivePlayers, fiveRewards, IERC20(ERC20Mock(weth)), 1000
    );
    ContestManager(conMan).fundContest(0);
    vm.stopPrank();

    // Only player[0] claims — remainingRewards drops to 800
    vm.prank(fivePlayers[0]);
    Pot(contest).claimCut();

    vm.warp(block.timestamp + 91 days);
    vm.prank(user);
    ContestManager(conMan).closeContest(contest);

    // managerCut = 800 / 10 = 80
    // claimantCut = (800 - 80) / 5 = 144  ← divided by 5, not 1
    // distributed = 80 + 144 = 224
    // LOCKED = 800 - 224 = 576 tokens stuck in Pot forever
    assertGt(ERC20Mock(weth).balanceOf(contest), 0);
}
```

### Recommended Mitigation

```diff
-   uint256 claimantCut = (remainingRewards - managerCut) / i_players.length;
-   for (uint256 i = 0; i < claimants.length; i++) {
-       _transferReward(claimants[i], claimantCut);
-   }
+   if (claimants.length > 0) {
+       uint256 claimantCut = (remainingRewards - managerCut) / claimants.length;
+       for (uint256 i = 0; i < claimants.length; i++) {
+           _transferReward(claimants[i], claimantCut);
+       }
+   }
+   // Sweep rounding dust and zero-claimant residual to the manager
+   uint256 residual = i_token.balanceOf(address(this));
+   if (residual > 0) {
+       i_token.transfer(msg.sender, residual);
+   }
```

