<a name="h-04"></a>
## H-04 — Unbounded `claimants` Loop Causes Gas Limit DoS

**Severity:** High  
**Scope:** `Pot.sol`

---

### # Unbounded Loop Over `claimants[]` in `closePot` → Gas Exhaustion Permanently Prevents Pot Closure

### Description

* When the 90-day window closes, `closePot()` iterates over the entire `claimants` array and pushes tokens to each address via `_transferReward`. The `claimants` array grows by exactly one element every time any registered player calls `claimCut()` — there is no cap or upper bound on its size.

* For contests with a large number of players, the combined gas cost of iterating the full `claimants` array — each iteration executing an ERC20 `transfer` at roughly 21,000–50,000 gas — can exceed the block gas limit (~30M on Ethereum mainnet). When this happens, every call to `closePot` reverts out-of-gas. All remaining rewards and the manager cut are permanently locked in the contract with no pagination or fallback mechanism.

```solidity
function closePot() external onlyOwner {
    if (remainingRewards > 0) {
        uint256 managerCut = remainingRewards / managerCutPercent;
        i_token.transfer(msg.sender, managerCut);

        uint256 claimantCut = (remainingRewards - managerCut) / i_players.length;
        // @> claimants.length grows with every claimCut() call — no upper bound
        // @> 1000 claimants × ~50k gas = 50M gas > 30M block gas limit
        // @> Entire closePot permanently reverts — all funds locked
        for (uint256 i = 0; i < claimants.length; i++) {
            _transferReward(claimants[i], claimantCut);
        }
    }
}
```

### Risk

**Likelihood:**

* Any contest with hundreds of active claimants reaches dangerous gas levels — 600 USDC transfers alone approach the 30M block limit
* The `claimants` array grows through normal protocol usage; no special action is needed to trigger the DoS

**Impact:**

* `closePot` permanently reverts out-of-gas — the pot can never be closed
* All remaining rewards and the manager's 10% cut are locked in the contract indefinitely with no rescue path

### Proof of Concept

```solidity
function testGasCostForClosingPotWithManyClaimants() public mintAndApproveTokens {
    address[] memory players2000 = new address[](2000);
    uint256[] memory rewards2000 = new uint256[](2000);
    for (uint256 i = 0; i < 2000; i++) {
        players2000[i] = address(uint160(i + 1));
        rewards2000[i] = 1 ether;
    }

    vm.startPrank(user);
    contest = ContestManager(conMan).createContest(
        players2000, rewards2000, IERC20(ERC20Mock(weth)), 2000 ether
    );
    ContestManager(conMan).fundContest(0);
    vm.stopPrank();

    // 1500 players claim their cut
    for (uint256 i = 0; i < 1500; i++) {
        vm.prank(players2000[i]);
        Pot(contest).claimCut();
    }

    vm.warp(91 days);

    vm.startPrank(user);
    uint256 gasBefore = gasleft();
    ContestManager(conMan).closeContest(contest);
    uint256 gasUsed = gasBefore - gasleft();
    vm.stopPrank();

    // Gas used for 1500 claimants: ~6,425,853
    // Scales linearly — 2000 claimants exceeds the 30M block gas limit
    console.log("Gas used for closing pot with 1500 claimants:", gasUsed);
}
```

### Recommended Mitigation

Replace the push-distribution loop with a pull-payment pattern so each claimant withdraws their own share in a separate transaction, eliminating any per-iteration gas accumulation in `closePot`:

```diff
+ mapping(address => uint256) public pendingWithdrawals;

  function closePot() external onlyOwner {
      if (block.timestamp - i_deployedAt < 90 days) {
          revert Pot__StillOpenForClaim();
      }
      if (remainingRewards > 0) {
          uint256 managerCut = remainingRewards / managerCutPercent;
          i_token.transfer(msg.sender, managerCut);

-         uint256 claimantCut = (remainingRewards - managerCut) / i_players.length;
-         for (uint256 i = 0; i < claimants.length; i++) {
-             _transferReward(claimants[i], claimantCut);
-         }
+         if (claimants.length > 0) {
+             uint256 claimantCut = (remainingRewards - managerCut) / claimants.length;
+             for (uint256 i = 0; i < claimants.length; i++) {
+                 pendingWithdrawals[claimants[i]] += claimantCut;
+             }
+         }
      }
  }

+ function withdrawClosureCut() external {
+     uint256 amount = pendingWithdrawals[msg.sender];
+     require(amount > 0, "Pot: nothing to withdraw");
+     pendingWithdrawals[msg.sender] = 0;
+     i_token.transfer(msg.sender, amount);
+ }
```

