<a name="m-01"></a>
## M-01 — Zero Claimants in `closePot` Locks 90% of Remaining Rewards

**Severity:** Medium  
**Scope:** `Pot.sol`

---

### # Empty `claimants[]` Array Causes Distribution Loop to Never Execute → 90% of Rewards Locked

### Description

* After the 90-day window, `closePot()` sends the manager their 10% cut, then distributes the remaining 90% among the `claimants` array — players who previously called `claimCut()`. The loop iterating over `claimants` is the only distribution mechanism for the claimant share.

* When no player has called `claimCut()` before the pot closes, `claimants.length == 0` and the loop body never executes. The manager receives `remainingRewards / 10` (which is sent to `ContestManager` instead of the owner per H-01), while the remaining 90% of `remainingRewards` stays permanently in the Pot contract. There is no fallback path, no second close attempt, and no rescue function.

```solidity
function closePot() external onlyOwner {
    if (remainingRewards > 0) {
        uint256 managerCut = remainingRewards / managerCutPercent;
        i_token.transfer(msg.sender, managerCut); // @> 10% transferred (to wrong address per H-01)

        uint256 claimantCut = (remainingRewards - managerCut) / i_players.length;
        // @> If claimants.length == 0, this loop body NEVER runs
        for (uint256 i = 0; i < claimants.length; i++) {
            _transferReward(claimants[i], claimantCut);
        }
        // @> No else branch — 90% of remainingRewards has no destination and stays in Pot
    }
}
```

### Risk

**Likelihood:**

* Any contest where all players miss the 90-day window triggers the full lock — not a rare edge case in a protocol explicitly designed around the possibility of missed claims
* Low-visibility contests or those with poor user notifications can easily reach closure with zero claimants

**Impact:**

* 90% of the total reward pool is permanently locked in the Pot contract with no recovery mechanism
* Combined with H-01, effectively 100% of `remainingRewards` is inaccessible after `closeContest` — 10% locked in `ContestManager`, 90% locked in `Pot`

### Proof of Concept

```solidity
function testClosePotWithZeroClaimants() public mintAndApproveTokens {
    vm.startPrank(user);
    contest = ContestManager(conMan).createContest(
        players, rewards, IERC20(weth), totalRewards
    );
    ContestManager(conMan).fundContest(0);
    vm.stopPrank();

    // No player calls claimCut — all 90 days pass with zero claims
    vm.warp(block.timestamp + 91 days);

    uint256 managerBalanceBefore = weth.balanceOf(user);

    vm.prank(user);
    ContestManager(conMan).closeContest(contest);

    // Owner received nothing (H-01 — cut went to ContestManager)
    assertEq(weth.balanceOf(user), managerBalanceBefore);
    // 90% of totalRewards permanently locked in Pot
    assertEq(weth.balanceOf(contest), (totalRewards * 90) / 100);
}
```

### Recommended Mitigation

```diff
+ if (claimants.length == 0) {
+     // No one claimed — return everything to the manager
+     i_token.transfer(msg.sender, remainingRewards - managerCut);
+ } else {
      uint256 claimantCut = (remainingRewards - managerCut) / claimants.length;
      for (uint256 i = 0; i < claimants.length; i++) {
          _transferReward(claimants[i], claimantCut);
      }
+ }
```

