<a name="m-02"></a>
## M-02 — `claimCut` Callable Before `fundContest` Shrinks Effective Claim Window

**Severity:** Medium  
**Scope:** `Pot.sol` · `ContestManager.sol`

---

### # 90-Day Timer Starts at Deployment, Not Funding → Shortened Claim Window and Failed Early Claims

### Description

* The `Pot` constructor records `i_deployedAt = block.timestamp`, starting the 90-day claim window immediately at deployment. `fundContest()` in `ContestManager` is a completely separate call that transfers tokens into the Pot — it can be executed any time after deployment, or never at all. The two operations are fully decoupled with no on-chain enforcement linking them.

* Players calling `claimCut()` before `fundContest` is executed receive an opaque ERC20 balance revert even though their `playersToRewards` entry is valid. More critically, every day the funding is delayed permanently removes a day from the legitimate claim window. A pot funded 30 days late silently gives players only 60 days to claim — with no on-chain signal that the effective deadline has shifted. The commented-out line in the constructor (`// i_token.transfer(address(this), i_totalRewards)`) is a direct indication that atomic self-funding was originally intended but was removed.

```solidity
// Pot.sol
constructor(address[] memory players, uint256[] memory rewards, IERC20 token, uint256 totalRewards) {
    // @> 90-day countdown begins immediately at construction
    i_deployedAt = block.timestamp;

    // @> Self-funding removed — Pot starts with 0 token balance
    // i_token.transfer(address(this), i_totalRewards);
}

// ContestManager.sol
function createContest(...) public onlyOwner returns (address) {
    // @> Timer starts the moment the Pot is deployed here
    Pot pot = new Pot(players, rewards, token, totalRewards);
    contests.push(address(pot));
    contestToTotalRewards[address(pot)] = totalRewards;
    // @> No funding — completely separate optional step with no deadline
    return address(pot);
}

function fundContest(uint256 index) public onlyOwner {
    // @> Can be called days or weeks after createContest, or never
    token.transferFrom(msg.sender, address(pot), totalRewards);
}
```

### Risk

**Likelihood:**

* Any deployment workflow that separates `createContest` and `fundContest` — common in multi-step scripts or manual operations — begins eroding the effective claim window from the first block
* Players monitoring `createContest` events and attempting to claim immediately will receive confusing ERC20 errors with no protocol-level explanation

**Impact:**

* Delayed funding silently reduces the effective claim window with no on-chain signal — players lose claimable time they are unaware of
* Players calling `claimCut()` on an unfunded pot receive a generic `ERC20InsufficientBalance` error instead of a meaningful protocol revert, creating poor UX and potential trust issues with the protocol

### Proof of Concept

```solidity
function testClaimCutRevertsBeforeFunding() public {
    vm.prank(owner);
    address potAddr = contestManager.createContest(
        players, rewards, token, 1000
    );
    // fundContest NOT called — Pot has 0 token balance

    // Player tries to claim immediately after contest creation
    vm.prank(players[0]);
    vm.expectRevert(); // Generic ERC20InsufficientBalance — no Pot error
    Pot(potAddr).claimCut();
}

function testDelayedFundingShrinkClaimWindow() public {
    vm.prank(owner);
    address potAddr = contestManager.createContest(
        players, rewards, token, 1000
    );

    // Owner funds 30 days after deployment
    vm.warp(block.timestamp + 30 days);
    vm.prank(owner);
    contestManager.fundContest(0);

    // Players effectively have only 60 days to claim, not 90
    // 61 more days and the owner can already close the pot
    vm.warp(block.timestamp + 61 days);
    vm.prank(owner);
    // Succeeds — 91 days since DEPLOYMENT, players had only 60 days from FUNDING
    contestManager.closeContest(potAddr);
}
```

### Recommended Mitigation

**Option A — Fund atomically at creation (recommended):**

```diff
  function createContest(
      address[] memory players,
      uint256[] memory rewards,
      IERC20 token,
      uint256 totalRewards
  ) public onlyOwner returns (address) {
      Pot pot = new Pot(players, rewards, token, totalRewards);
      contests.push(address(pot));
      contestToTotalRewards[address(pot)] = totalRewards;
+     token.transferFrom(msg.sender, address(pot), totalRewards);
      return address(pot);
  }
```

**Option B — Gate `claimCut` behind a funded flag:**

```diff
+ bool private s_isFunded;

+ modifier onlyFunded() {
+     if (!s_isFunded) revert Pot__InsufficientFunds();
+     _;
+ }

+ function markFunded() external onlyOwner {
+     s_isFunded = true;
+ }

- function claimCut() public {
+ function claimCut() public onlyFunded {
      address player = msg.sender;
      uint256 reward = playersToRewards[player];
      if (reward <= 0) revert Pot__RewardNotFound();
      playersToRewards[player] = 0;
      remainingRewards -= reward;
      claimants.push(player);
      _transferReward(player, reward);
  }
```

